{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949105-reworking-the-centimani-the-resistance","id":949105,"title":"Reworking the Centimani: The Resistance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-11T21:45:50-07:00","id":949105,"title":"Reworking the Centimani: The Resistance","content":"So, I've been struggling with how to handle the Centimani for a while, and I was contemplating jettisoning them entirely. But I had an idea from another project I was working on. Dark Eras 2 made me think of the idea of future or alternate history Dark Eras, and I came up with a retro-futuristic one for Promethean based on classic scifi, The Protomen, and Janelle Monae. In it, the Centimani were an underground resistance movement of Prometheans and alchemists who helped those Prometheans who didn't want to submit to government-mandated Pilgrimages. <br /> <br /> So I'm considering turning the Centimani from a Refinement to the closest thing that the Created have to a society. The Centimani are a scattered network of Created and alchemists. Their numbers are very low, given the low numbers of the Created. They have no settlements- instead, one or a few Created and often several alchemists operate various way stations and laboratories connected to the loose Centimani network. The Centimani are more of an ideal than an organization, and still a sort of resistance movement. The Created are a disparate bunch, but the Centimani ideal is what allows them to come together. Of the Prometheans who identify as Centimani, a few are ambitious enough to dream or greater power or influence. Some want to increase their numbers through mass creation- this is the greatest source of conflict within the Promethean &quot;community&quot;, though it's more than this conflict inevitably manifests in any gathering of Prometheans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T13:12:51-07:00","id":950193,"title":"","content":"You... do realize that by the canon, even back in 1e, the very concept of &quot;government-mandated Pilgrimages&quot; is utterly inane? Though 1e did a bad job of reflecting it mechanically, a Pilgrimage is supposed to be a highly personal experience of growth and learning, and as such can't be forced on someone. Unless you're throwing canon entirely out the window, this is about as sensible as having a Buddhist-themed dystopia with &quot;government-mandated Enlightenment&quot; for very similar reasons. Or, keeping it within ChroD/WoD, government-mandated Golconda for vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2836-nezumi","name":"Nezumi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T13:19:54-07:00","id":950194,"title":"","content":"How exactly is a &quot;government-mandated pilgrimage&quot; supposed to work? Are they created by the government? How and why would the government be forcing Prometheans to undertake a journey to humanity?<br /> <br /> Are these Centimani meant to resemble their book counterparts in anything but name or are they just repurposing the label?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T14:21:49-07:00","id":950220,"title":"","content":"I think this is for gecko's Lightning Campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T16:36:55-07:00","id":950305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nezumi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949105-reworking-the-centimani-the-resistance?p=950193#post950193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You... do realize that by the canon, even back in 1e, the very concept of &amp;quot;government-mandated Pilgrimages&amp;quot; is utterly inane? Though 1e did a bad job of reflecting it mechanically, a Pilgrimage is supposed to be a highly personal experience of growth and learning, and as such can't be forced on someone. Unless you're throwing canon entirely out the window, this is about as sensible as having a Buddhist-themed dystopia with &amp;quot;government-mandated Enlightenment&amp;quot; for very similar reasons. Or, keeping it within ChroD/WoD, government-mandated Golconda for vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dystopias often don't make sense. I'm not saying that government-mandated Pilgrimages would even work well. In fact, the fact that Pilgrimages are personal means that even Prometheans who wanted to become human would want to oppose the regime. <br /> <br /> Also, how can you type the words&quot; government-mandated enlightenment&quot; and not think &quot;holy shit, that's an awesome story hook?<br /> <br /> My other post explains things about the future setting better, but basically the government made pilgrimages mandatory as a way to keep Prometheans from being a threat while also seeming compassionate. The way it works is, if you can't provide proof you're spending as much time and effort as possible to become human, you're detained and possibly executed. <br /> <br /> And these Centimani resemble their earlier version in a very fundamental way: they're all about coming to terms with being a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}